// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/course/lesson_01_fpga_intro.t27 -- lesson 1 of FPGA course v2, "What is an FPGA?",
// as seven story snapshots on the T27F visual factory contract.
//
// WHY. Course v2 (specs/course/fpga_course_v2.t27) replaces the self-marked lesson with the
// loop of specs/course/mastery.t27: PREDICT -> POKE -> EXPLAIN -> TRANSFER -> PROVE. This
// file is the first lesson written against that loop, spec first, before any page shows it.
// Each step of the lesson is one scene: a VfGraph of specs/t27f/visual_factory_contract.t27
// (T27F-002) that must pass vf_validate, with one focused control and test ids that a page
// test can find.
//
// THE SEVEN SCENES, in order: hook, visual, predict, poke, explain, transfer, prove.
//   hook      the question: 134,600 LUT6 on the board, 215,360 logic cells in the data sheet.
//   visual    the ALINX AX7203 board facts and the XC7A200T fabric totals.
//   predict   how many input patterns a LUT6 has; the reader commits to a number.
//   poke      six input toggles on one LUT6 that holds a 6-input AND; the output follows.
//   explain   slices -> LUT6 -> logic cells, with the arithmetic shown.
//   transfer  the 1.6 ratio on an FPGA the lesson did not show (a made-up count, no part).
//   prove     a value read from specs/boards/ax7203.t27, checked against an answer key.
//
// STORY SNAPSHOT. A snapshot row has the fields of VF_SNAPSHOT_FIELDS (T27F-002): index,
// kind, rect, role, name, focus, test_id. snap_row() fills all of them except rect, and
// rect_known stays false: snap_row does not call the layout engine. vf_layout (T27F-003,
// #13242) and the story snapshot of T27F-004 (#13245) are on master now; the rects of these
// scenes come from specs/course/lesson_01_frames_main.t27, which lays out and renders them.
//
// SOURCES. Every board number comes from specs/boards/ax7203.t27 (part and IDCODE from
// fpga/HARDWARE_SSOT.md, fabric totals from AMD DS180), and a test ties each number a scene
// shows to the board constant. The loop, the streak and the review days come from
// specs/course/mastery.t27. Every scene string passes the drift rules of
// specs/tri/course/audit.t27.
//
// NOT CLAIMED: no rects here, no page. Frames exist (lesson_01_frames_main.t27), but nobody has looked at them, so
// nothing here says they look right. No learner has used the lesson. The transfer FPGA is
// hypothetical and is not a real part.
// ASCII only (L3). phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

